I see a critical issue! Looking at the `move_object` function at line 479-487:

```rust
// Reset battlefield-specific state when leaving the battlefield.
if from == Zone::Battlefield && to != Zone::Battlefield {
    obj.tapped = false;
    obj.summoning_sick = false;
    obj.damage_marked = 0;
    obj.dealt_deathtouch_damage = false; obj.damaged_by.clear();
    obj.attached_to = None;
    obj.counters.clear();
    obj.regeneration_shields = 0;


}
```

When a creature leaves the battlefield, the function clears standard counters, but it's not clearing `card_state` — so if a card like Ludevic's Test Subject gets bounced back to hand with hatchling counters still stored, those counters would persist when it re-enters the battlefield, violating MTG rules that treat a permanent re-entering as a new object with no counters.

I'm also noticing that `is_transformed` isn't being reset either when a permanent leaves the battlefield, which means a transformed card would stay transformed even after leaving and re-entering play. I need to check whether `is_transformed` gets reset anywhere else in the codebase, since this could be a broader issue affecting all double-faced cards in the engine.

